```python
class Solution:
    def maxSum(self, nums: list[int], k: int) -> int:
        nums.sort(reverse=True)
        n = len(nums)
        # The maximum number of elements we can effectively gather into a contiguous subarray is min(n, k + 1)
        # because each swap can bring one additional large element into the subarray.
        return sum(nums[:min(n, k + 1)])
```
